      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "🚨 **BLOCKING: the new lint-guard test fails on the canonical dmtools runner**

`listJsEntries` parses the `file_list` result unconditionally:

```js
return JSON.parse(file_list({ path: dir })).entries.filter(function (p) {
```

On the dmtools-java runner, `file_list` returns an **object** (host value), not a JSON string, so `JSON.parse` throws `unexpected token: '[REDACTED:Sensitive Value]'` and the suite goes red:

```
dmtools run js/unit-tests/run_all.json
❌ ... lint guard: zero non-test js/ files call createTracker(null or initTracker(null
   unexpected token: '[REDACTED:Sensitive Value]'
{"success":false,"passed":5801,"failed":1}
```

(verified by running the canonical runner against this PR's head). The repo's existing file_list consumers guard the shape — see `js/unit-tests/test_packRequirePath.js:162,176` and `test_instructionRefs.js:66,101`:

```js
var raw = file_list({ path: dir });
if (typeof raw === 'string') raw = JSON.parse(raw);
return ((raw && raw.entries) || []).filter(function (p) { return /\.js$/.test(String(p)); });
```

Please apply the same guard — as written, this test fails the canonical green gate the moment the PR merges.

*(Side note, same test: it also fails for a subtler reason — `triggerBitriseTestAutomation.js` still passes a null config, aliased through `var initialConfig = null`, so the guard's syntactic regex is green while the anti-pattern it targets is still present. See the separate comment on that file.)*"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "rootCommentId": 4350722828,
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORYAuYs6vRqtO",
      "path": "js/createRepoTasks.js",
      "line": 27,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "🚨 **BLOCKING: `loadProjectConfig(params)` is called with the full action params — `jobParams.customParams` / `jobParams.configPath` are silently dropped**

This new helper (duplicated in ~17 files: `checkWipLabel.js`, `createQuestionsAndAssignForReview.js`, `createRepoTasks.js`, `createRepoTasksMulti.js`, `createSolutionDesignTicketsAndAssignForReview.js`, `enhanceSDAPIDescriptionAndAssess.js`, `enhanceSolutionDesignDescriptionAndAssess.js`, `fetchLinkedBugsToInput.js`, `fetchLinkedTestsToInput.js`, `finalizeBugFixBatchMerge.js` (via `actualParams`), `intakePreAction.js`, `redirectToRepoAgent.js`, `workflowFailureReporter.js`, `createPlannedStoriesFromOutput.js`, `postTestReviewComments.js`, `preCliTestReworkSetup.js`, `writeSolutionAndLabels.js`) passes the raw action `params` object:

```js
function resolveProjectConfig(params) {
    return configLoader ? configLoader.loadProjectConfig(params) : null;
}
```

`loadProjectConfig` reads only `params.customParams` and `params.configPath` (`js/configLoader.js:717`, `:535-541`). In the standard Teammate runtime shape the action receives `{ jobParams: {...}, ticket: {...} }` as **sibling top-level keys** — `configLoader.js:507-513` documents this explicitly ("Most call sites use `params.jobParams || params` ... which silently drops the sibling `params.ticket`", and the same applies to `jobParams.customParams`/`configPath` here). So for every one of these call sites:

- `jobParams.customParams.configPath` and `jobParams.configPath` (per-rule project config override in multi-project SM orchestration) are missed → the **default-repo** `.dmtools/config.js` loads instead → the wrong `tracker.provider` can still win — i.e. the exact gh-1163 failure mode this PR fixes survives in that deployment mode;
- `customParams.targetRepository` is ignored by `applyTargetRepository` (`configLoader.js`) → `config.repository.owner/repo` stay empty → on GitHub-tracker deployments the tracker is built without owner/repo (bare issue-number expansion breaks) for all of these agents;
- `customParams.scmProvider` / `featureBranchEnabled` overrides (`applyCustomParamOverrides`) and the `branchNamingFnPath` / `prSearchFnPath` hooks are also skipped.

The same PR already uses the correct shape in several files — `mergeStoryTestAutomationPR.js:465` (`params.jobParams || params`), `notifyBugMerged.js:46`, `postMobileTestAutomationResults.js:630`, `postTestAutomationResults.js:659`, and `trackers.js`'s own `resolveProjectConfig` (via `_extractJobParams`). Please make all the copies thread the same shape, ideally reusing the exported helper that also re-attaches `ticket` for resolver hooks:

```js
function resolveProjectConfig(params) {
    if (!configLoader) return null;
    try {
        return configLoader.loadProjectConfig(configLoader.paramsForConfigLoad(params));
    } catch (e) {
        return null;
    }
}
```

That would also collapse the ~17 divergent one-off copies into one consistent convention."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "rootCommentId": 4350723292,
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORYAuYs6vRqxh",
      "path": "js/triggerBitriseTestAutomation.js",
      "line": 352,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `var initialConfig = null;` renames the anti-pattern instead of fixing it**

```js
var initialConfig = null;
tracker = trackersModule.createTracker(initialConfig, resolveInitialTrackerCustomParams(params));
```

This only renames the literal `null` so the new `createTracker(null` / `initTracker(null` lint regex in `test_trackers.js` stays green — the config passed is still null, and the bootstrap tracker works solely thanks to the internal best-effort `_resolveEffectiveConfig` fallback. The PR description states all affected files now "Loaded `projectConfig` via `configLoader.loadProjectConfig(...)` and passed it to `initTracker(config, ...)` / `createTracker(config, ...)`" — this file does not.

`configLoader` is already imported at the top of this file (line 26) and loaded 7 lines later anyway (`var projectConfig = configLoader.loadProjectConfig(params.jobParams || params);`). Just hoist that load above the bootstrap tracker creation and pass it to both `createTracker` calls — that removes the null-config window, matches the stated PR intent, and keeps the lint guard honest."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "rootCommentId": 4350723864,
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORYAuYs6vRq22",
      "path": "js/configLoader.js",
      "line": 1079,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "💡 **SUGGESTION: tracker-precedence order now differs between the three resolvers**

After this PR there are three provider-precedence orders in the codebase:

1. `trackers.js _rawProviderCandidate` — `customParams.trackerProvider` → `config.tracker.provider` → `DEFAULT_TRACKER` env → `config.defaultTracker` (project config **above** env).
2. `configLoader.resolveTrackerType` (this diff) — `DEFAULT_TRACKER` env → `config.tracker.provider` → `config.defaultTracker` (env **above** config).
3. `writeSolutionAndLabels.detectTrackerType` (this diff) — `DEFAULT_TRACKER` env → `tracker.provider()` → `'jira'` (env **above** config; note the PR description says "consult `tracker.provider()` first", but env is still checked first).

When `DEFAULT_TRACKER` and the project's `tracker.provider` disagree, `createTracker` builds one provider (e.g. ado) while `resolveTrackerType` picks prompt files and `detectTrackerType` routes markup for another (e.g. jira). Both env-first orders are pre-existing; nothing here regresses. But now that project config is consulted in more places, it would be cheap to align (or explicitly document) the single source of truth — the canonical order is the one in the `trackers.js` header comment."
    },
    {
